/// The MemQL OS shell, as the platform's own site (memql#4705).
///
/// SEEDED, not special-cased. The OS is how a cluster is managed, so if it
/// were an ordinary row the cluster would ship with an empty site table and no
/// way to reach the screen that fills it. Seeding resolves that without a
/// branch in the serving path -- and re-seeding at boot means an operator
/// cannot brick cluster management by deleting the row.
///
/// It is the SECOND inhabitant of this slot and the only one left: the MemQL
/// Portal was site #1 (memql#3711) and epic memql#4984 retired it, so
/// everything below was true of the portal first and is true of the OS now.
///
/// A named front-door host, not a wildcard site: exact Ingress, exact
/// Certificate SAN, HTTP-01. Putting it on *.<domain> would send Safari
/// through edge site-hosting with no SAN (memql#4224).
///
/// bundleRef is file:///app/os -- the directory the image already ships. That
/// is the whole of the difference between "in the image" and "in storage": a
/// URI scheme.
///
/// status is "live" and systemOwned is true -- createSite's ordinary caller
/// gets "draft" / false; the shell needs both flipped at materialization time,
/// which is why createSite (dsl/platform/mutations.memql) accepts them as
/// optional args instead of hardcoding the operator-created-site defaults.
///
/// The hostname is the committed localhost default, carried the same way the
/// Ingress hosts are (memql#3593); SeedMaterializer rewrites it from
/// MEMQL_DOMAIN, so an install on another domain overrides it through the same
/// seam.
///
/// NO ownerUserId, and its ABSENCE is the meaning (memql#4344): an empty owner
/// is the CLUSTER-OWNED state, which is what the platform's own site has to be
/// -- it is the platform's row, not whichever principal happened to boot the
/// cluster. createSite stamps `ownerUserId: actor.userId` like every owned
/// concept must, and executeWrite undoes that stamp for a system actor, so
/// adding the field here would be both unnecessary and wrong. `os.<domain>` is
/// also a RESERVED label a user may not claim, and the same privileged path is
/// what lets this seed use it (component/memql/platform_site_hostname_policy.go).
@description("The MemQL OS shell")
seed site os {
  id:          "os"
  hostname:    "os.memql.localhost"
  kind:        "spa"
  bundleRef:   "file:///app/os"
  status:      "live"
  apiProxy:    true
  systemOwned: true
  title:       "MemQL OS"
}
